(Infrastructure AI evaluates physical roadway defects detected by the computer vision engines. Its pipeline executes in seven) Tj
T* (sequential steps:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
45.354330708661422 395.4907086614172727 Td
(1. CV Observation: Receives bounding box, cavity length, width, and depth estimations from potholeEngine.) Tj
T* (2. Operational Context: Correlates defect location with corridor bus traffic density and road classification.) Tj
T* (3. RAG Evidence: Queries IRC:82-2015 for severity categorization and recommended patch specifications.) Tj
T* (4. Risk Interpretation: Categorizes defect into CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW based on cavity depth and traffic exposure.) Tj
T* (5. Recommendation Formulation: Suggests repair technique \(e.g., VG-30 hot-mix asphalt infill with mechanical compaction\)) Tj
T* (and SLA deadline \(24 hours for transit corridors\).) Tj
T* (6. Missing Information Flagging: Explicitly identifies parameters absent from the visual feed \(e.g., subgrade moisture levels,) Tj
T* (underlying drainage failure, recent rain logs\) to prevent premature engineering conclusions.) Tj
T* (7. Human Review Enqueueing: Pushes the structured recommendation to the municipal review queue for engineer sign-off.) Tj
ET
BT
